## Q5 — Dimensional Analysis (4 marks)
**Spec ref**: MA1, MA2
### Question
When a sphere of radius r metres is falling at v m s⁻¹ it experiences an air resistance force F newtons.
The force is modelled as F = kr^α v^β, where k is a constant with units kg m⁻².
**(a)** State the dimensions of F. [1 mark]
**(b)** Use dimensional analysis to find the value of α and the value of β. [3 marks]
### Solution
**(a)**
Force = mass × acceleration
$$[F] = \text{MLT}^{-2}$$
**(b)**
$$[F] = [k][r]^\alpha[v]^\beta$$
$$\text{MLT}^{-2} = \text{ML}^{-2} \times \text{L}^\alpha \times (\text{LT}^{-1})^\beta$$
$$\text{MLT}^{-2} = \text{ML}^{-2+\alpha+\beta}\text{T}^{-\beta}$$
Comparing powers:
**M**: 1 = 1 ✓
**T**: −2 = −β → **β = 2**
**L**: 1 = −2 + α + β → 1 = −2 + α + 2 → **α = 1**
### Answer
**α = 1, β = 2**
So the model is F = krv².
